  "scope": [
    "Finite feature covariance projection, nonnegative white discrepancies, head blocks, source/role replacement and between-component mixture PSD.",
    "Mean and covariance restriction identities; physical-policy white terms agree with index diagonals on the distinct-policy pools enforced by the implementation.",
    "Fixed affine risk identity derived from actual Bochner integrals on any probability space, using explicit first and centered mixed second moments and aStar S = c.",
    "The covariance of these centered observations is PSD by the integral of a square; relationship mismatch is consequently nonnegative."
  ],
  "external_assumptions": [
    "Coefficient and task covariances are given symmetric PSD inputs; white variances and weights are nonnegative. A probability-mixture interpretation additionally requires normalized weights and their weighted mean.",
    "The physical-policy index is injective where a white term is implemented by the index identity matrix.",
    "Source affine coefficients and centers are fixed conditional on source assets. The covariance, cross moments and expectations in the MSE identity belong to the specified target law.",
    "The MSE theorem assumes integrable U and Y, integrable centered pairwise products and target square, and the reference normal equations; it does not assume Gaussianity."
  ],
  "remaining_boundaries": [
    "Finite Gaussian law construction, the Gaussian regression/sampling pivots and noncentral-t laws are not newly formalized here.",
    "Floating-point source-fit validity, numerical moments/quantiles, reconstruction/encoder/loading error constants and nonlinear AFTER performance are outside these two modules.",
    "The inverse-matrix expression aStar = c S^-1 remains the mathematical specialization when S is invertible; the Lean risk identity uses its normal equations directly."
  ],
